+# Electric hood corrected against the reference — 2026-10-29
+
+EHR01: The owner's side and front views show an over-rounded hood, with a raised rear hump and a swollen transverse section. Compared with the supplied silver-car reference, the desired shape has a restrained centre, more defined shoulders, and one clean fall toward the nose. EHR02 retains the current windshield foot, cabin, rear geometry, factory/saved paint and handling.
+
+The active car now uses `electric_reference_body.gd`, independently of the older `electric_coachwork.gd`. This task changes the active front shoulder's S-shaped height blend to a convex quadratic profile, reduces the hood's front crown coefficient from90 to38mm in authored model coordinates, replaces the pinched square-root transverse section with a quadratic section, and concentrates the paired shoulder ridges and shallow valleys. The cowl still meets the unchanged windshield foot at `(0,1,-0.9)`. Front fenders, fascia and light guide share the same authored surface and follow the corrected hood instead of leaving an open seam.
+
+[Matched native comparison](evidence/electric-hood-reference-correction-2026-10-29/before-after.html). Side, head-on, bonnet and front-quarter views are included, with clean and synthetic-wear finishes. The reference is visual guidance; no image pixels or external geometry are incorporated.
+
+Runtime scope is the body source plus the prepared-root constant in `electric_reference_mesh.gd`. New meshes use the separate `electric_reference_hood_v1` directory. A concurrent v2-to-v3 preparation change was already occurring during inspection; that work is preserved. The final hood audit uses v3 control meshes whose manifest must match the exact task-start body-source hash. The first audit used the older v2 control and reported two flattening failures; its measurements/log remain. The final control selection and its source-hash assertion correct the comparison without relaxing the numerical checks. Intermediate render/source candidates remain separately archived.
+
+Final actual-buffer15/0, procedural nose64/0, prepared nose64/0, native model15/0, actual App58/0, racing23/0 and owned parsing pass. The12.4mm world-scale hump above the cowl is removed. The absolute front-centre/outer-corner difference falls59.1to16.9mm; the corrected centreline rises continuously toward the unchanged cowl. Visible full/simple geometry remains116832/34104 triangles, with3296 shadow triangles. All221 prepared meshes, the Volt template and52 pictures refresh, with16 final captures per renderer and16 matched controls. The actual-buffer regression checks that the hood has no hump above its cowl, its front section is substantially flatter than the exact control, its centreline is monotonic and convex, and its cowl position is unchanged, in full/simple models. Existing nose tests separately check the actual hood/fascia seam, visible lamps and physically open bumper recesses on generated and prepared meshes. Existing native model, actual Garage/race and focused racing checks cover integration. [Actual measurements/results](evidence/electric-hood-reference-correction-2026-10-29/report.json) and [commands/exits](evidence/electric-hood-reference-correction-2026-10-29/commands.json) record the completed checks.
+
+Prepared meshes, shadows, the Volt Garage template and52 native Garage/header/news/livery pictures refresh through the pinned engine and isolated profile. Historical v2/v3 assets and car configurations are protected. The [task-only patch](evidence/electric-hood-reference-correction-2026-10-29/task.patch) and [forward/reverse proof](evidence/electric-hood-reference-correction-2026-10-29/checkpoint.json) retain concurrent manifest context and exclude unrelated model/cache work and generated build identities.
+
+Reload/rebuild and owner appearance acceptance remain. No physical-device query/test, APK, owner-save/live/backend mutation, deployment, owner-process restart or shared-index staging/commit/merge was performed. No exact-photograph, aerodynamic, phone-performance or full-project parser claim is made. Desktop App hitches remain outside this geometry correction.
